{title: 612 - Onward, Christian Soldiers!}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #612 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 612}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]Onward Christian [Em7]sol[A7]diers! Marching [Bm]as [A7]to [D]war,
[D]With the cross of [Em7]Je[A7]sus [E7]Going on be[A]fore.
[A]Christ, the royal [D]Master, Leads against the [G]foe;
[G]For[D]ward [G]in[D]to [G]ba[D]t[G]tl[D]e, [G]See, [D]His [A7]ban[D]ners [A]go!
[D]Onward, Christian [Em7]soldiers! [A7]Marching as to [D]war,
[D]With the [Em]cross of [D]Jesus, [G]Going [A7]on be[D]fore.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[D]Onward, [Em7]Christian [A7]soldiers, [Bm]marching [A7]as [D]to war,
[D]with [Em7]the cross [A7]of [E7]Jesus going [A]on before.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]Like [Em7]a mighty [A7]army [Bm]moves the [A7]church [D]of God;
[D]brothers, [Em7]we are [A7]treading where [E7]the saints [A]have trod.
[A]We are [D]not divided, all [G]one body we,
[G][D]one [G][D]in [G]hope [D][G]and [D][G]doctrine, [D]one [A7][D]in [A]charity.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]Crowns [Em7]and thrones [A7]my [Bm]perish, kingdoms [A7]rise [D]and wane,
[D]but [Em7]the church [A7]of [E7]Jesus constant [A]will remain.
[A]Gates of hell [D]can never 'gainst [G]that church prevail;
[G][D]we [G]have [D][G]Christ's [D]own [G][D]promise, [G]and [D][A7]that [D]cannot [A]fail.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[D]Onward [Em7]then, [A7]ye people, [Bm]join [A7]our [D]happy throng,
[D]blend [Em7]with ours [A7]your voices [E7]in the [A]triumph song.
[A]Glory, laud, [D]and honor unto [G]Christ the King,
[G][D]this [G][D]through [G]countless [D][G]ages [D][G]men [D]and [A7][D]angels [A]sing.
{end_of_verse}
